Q: how to give access rights to media directory for gonic on nixos A: <p>Found a working setup. To the config in the question I had to add:</p>
<p>Create a group that owns the media tree and add the gonic user to it</p>
<pre class="lang-hs prettyprint-override"><code>users.groups.media = { };
    users.users.gonic = {
    isSystemUser = true;
    group = &quot;media&quot;;
    description = &quot;Gonic media server&quot;;
};
</code></pre>
<p>Ensure the directories exist and are owned by the “media” group</p>
<pre class="lang-hs prettyprint-override"><code>systemd.tmpfiles.rules = [
    &quot;d /media 0755 root root -&quot;
    &quot;d /media/playlists 0755 root media -&quot;
    &quot;d /media/podcasts 0755 root media -&quot;
    &quot;d /media/music    0755 root media -&quot;
];
</code></pre>
